r B", "5": "Lower B"}'::jsonb, '{"b1":{"1":[["Flat Dumbbell Press",3,"8-12",120,true],["Seated Cable Row",3,"10-12",90,true],["Incline Dumbbell Press",3,"10-12",90,false],["Lat Pulldown",3,"10-12",90,true],["Dumbbell Lateral Raise",3,"12-15",60,false],["Dumbbell Curl",2,"12-15",60,false],["Cable Rope Pushdown",2,"12-15",60,false]],"2":[["Barbell Back Squat",3,"8-12",150,true],["Romanian Deadlift",3,"10-12",120,true],["Dumbbell Bulgarian Split Squat",2,"10-12 each leg",90,false],["Seated Leg Curl",3,"10-15",60,true],["Standing Calf Raise",3,"10-15",60,false],["Plank",2,"30-45 sec",45,false]],"4":[["Machine Chest Press",3,"10-12",90,true],["Chest-Supported Row",3,"10-12",90,true],["Neutral-Grip Lat Pulldown",3,"10-12",90,true],["Cable Fly",2,"12-15",60,false],["Reverse Pec Deck",3,"12-15",60,false],["Hammer Curl",2,"10-12",60,false],["Overhead Cable Extension",2,"12-15",60,false]],"5":[["Leg Press",3,"10-15",120,true],["Hip Thrust",3,"10-12",90,true],["Walking Lunge",2,"10-12 each leg",90,false],["Lying Leg Curl",3,"10-15",60,true],["Leg Extension",2,"12-15",60,false],["Seated Calf Raise",3,"12-15",60,false],["Dead Bug",2,"8-10 each side",45,false]]},"b2":{"1":[["Incline Barbell Press",3,"8-10",120,true],["Barbell Bent-Over Row",3,"8-10",120,true],["Flat Dumbbell Press",3,"10-12",90,false],["Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown",3,"10-12",90,true],["Leaning Cable Lateral Raise",3,"12-15",60,true],["Incline Dumbbell Curl",3,"10-12",60,false],["Overhead Cable Extension",3,"10-12",60,false]],"2":[["Barbell Back Squat",3,"8-10",150,true],["Romanian Deadlift",3,"8-10",150,true],["Leg Press",3,"12-15",120,false],["Seated Leg Curl",3,"10-12",60,true],["Standing Calf Raise",4,"10-12",60,false],["Hanging Knee Raise",2,"10-15",60,false]],"4":[["Machine Chest Press",3,"10-12",90,true],["Chest-Supported T-Bar Row",3,"10-12",90,true],["Close-Grip Lat Pulldown",3,"10-12",90,true],["Cable Fly",3,"12-15",60,false],["Dumbbell Lateral Raise",3,"12-15",60,false],["Cable Curl",2,"10-12",60,false],["Cable Rope Pushdown",2,"10-12",60,false]],"5":[["Dumbbell Bulgarian Split Squat",3,"8-12 each leg",90,true],["Hip Thrust",3,"8-12",120,true],["Lying Leg Curl",3,"10-12",60,true],["Leg Extension",3,"12-15",60,false],["Hip Adduction",2,"12-15",60,false],["Seated Calf Raise",3,"12-15",60,false],["Kneeling Cable Crunch",2,"12-15",60,false]]},"b3":{"1":[["Bench Press",4,"5-8",180,true],["Pendlay Row",4,"6-8",150,true],["Incline Dumbbell Press",3,"8-10",120,false],["Lat Pulldown",3,"8-10",90,true],["Dumbbell Lateral Raise",3,"10-15",60,false],["EZ-Bar Curl",2,"8-10",60,false],["Skull Crusher",2,"8-10",60,false]],"2":[["Barbell Back Squat",4,"5-8",180,true],["Romanian Deadlift",3,"6-8",150,true],["Dumbbell Bulgarian Split Squat",3,"8-10 each leg",90,false],["Seated Leg Curl",3,"8-10",75,false],["Standing Calf Raise",3,"8-12",60,false],["Pallof Press",2,"10 each side",45,false]],"4":[["Close-Grip Bench Press",3,"6-8",150,true],["Seated Cable Row",3,"8-10",90,true],["Chin-Up",3,"6-10",120,true],["Cable Fly",2,"10-12",60,false],["Reverse Pec Deck",3,"12-15",60,false],["Hammer Curl",2,"8-12",60,false],["Overhead Cable Extension",2,"10-12",60,false]],"5":[["Trap Bar Deadlift",3,"5-6",180,true],["Leg Press",3,"8-10",150,true],["Hip Thrust",3,"6-10",120,false],["Lying Leg Curl",3,"8-10",60,true],["Leg Extension",2,"10-12",60,false],["Seated Calf Raise",3,"10-12",60,false]]},"b4":{"1":[["Incline Dumbbell Press",3,"8-12",120,true],["Dumbbell Single-Arm Row",3,"10-12 each arm",90,true],["Machine Chest Press",3,"10-12",90,false],["Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown",3,"10-12",90,true],["Cable Low Single-Arm Lateral Raise",3,"12-20 each arm",45,true],["Bayesian Curl",3,"12-15 each arm",60,false],["Single-Arm Overhead Cable Extension",3,"12-15 each arm",60,false]],"2":[["Barbell Back Squat",3,"6-10",150,true],["Romanian Deadlift",3,"8-10",150,true],["Leg Extension",3,"12-20",60,false],["Seated Leg Curl",3,"10-15",60,true],["Standing Calf Raise",4,"10-15",60,false],["Kneeling Cable Crunch",2,"12-15",60,false]],"4":[["Flat Dumbbell Press",3,"8-12",90,true],["Chest-Supported Row",3,"10-12",90,true],["Neutral-Grip Lat Pulldown",3,"10-12",90,true],["Cable Low-to-High Fly",3,"12-15",60,false],["Machine Face Pull",3,"15-20",60,false],["Incline Dumbbell Curl",2,"10-15",60,false],["Cable Rope Pushdown",2,"12-15",60,false]],"5":[["Front-Foot-Elevated Split Squat",3,"10-12 each leg",90,true],["Leg Press",3,"12-15",120,true],["Hip Thrust",3,"10-12",90,false],["Lying Leg Curl",3,"12-15",60,true],["Hip Adduction",2,"12-15",60,false],["Seated Calf Raise",3,"15-20",45,false],["Hanging Knee Raise",2,"10-15",60,false]]}}'::jsonb);
select public.add_muscle_year('Muscle Year – 5 days a week', 'A 1-year muscle building program for 5 days a week (upper, lower, push, pull and legs, Monday to Friday). It''s built on the muscle research: each muscle is trained about twice a week, with 10-20 hard sets per muscle a week, sets taken close to failure and the weight going up whenever you hit the top of the rep range. It runs in four 3-month blocks of 13 weeks:
Block 1 (weeks 1-13), Foundation: learn every lift and build the habit. Moderate weights for 8-15 reps, stopping each set with 2-3 good reps left.
Block 2 (weeks 14-26), Volume: more sets for each muscle, 8-15 reps, stopping with 1-2 reps left. This is where most of the new muscle comes from.
Block 3 (weeks 27-39), Strength: heavier main lifts for 5-8 reps with longer rests, so you can lift more in block 4. Other exercises stay at 8-12 reps.
Block 4 (weeks 40-52), Peak: back to 8-20 reps, with exercises that stretch the muscle under load (incline curls, overhead extensions, deep leg presses). The last set of the small exercises can go to 1 rep short of failure.
Inside each block, sets go up on the main exercises in weeks 3 and 5 and again from week 10. Week 7 is a deload (half the sets, about 70% of the weight) and week 13 is a review week (half the sets: check your best weights, weigh in, take progress photos and recover before the next block). With 5 sessions, each muscle is trained twice a week, never on two days in a row, and the weekend is for recovery. Keep your form clean: add weight only when every rep in every set is done well. Can''t do a chin-up yet? Do it on the assisted pull-up machine. Recovery is part of the program: sleep 7-9 hours, take at least one full rest day a week, and use the Recovery section on your rest days. If your joints ache, you''re tired for days, or your lifts go down two sessions in a row, tell your coach so a deload week can come sooner.', 'Muscle is built from food. Work out your numbers in Nutrition > Muscle building: your BMR and macros: your BMR (what your body burns at rest), what you burn in a day with training, and your daily calories and macros. In short: eat about 5-10% more than your body uses (around 200-350 kcal a day), protein 1.6-2.2 g per kg of bodyweight split over 3-5 meals with 25-40 g each, fat at least 0.8 g per kg, and the rest from carbs (rice, potatoes, sweet potato, pap, bread, fruit, beans). Put most of your carbs in the meals before and after training. Weigh in every 2 weeks: aim to gain about 0.25-0.5% of your bodyweight a week (about 1-2 kg a month for most people). Gaining faster than that is mostly fat, so eat a bit less; not gaining, eat a bit more. Keep eating normally in deload and review weeks. Drink 35 ml of water per kg a day plus extra around training.', '5-8 minute warm-up: 3-4 minutes easy bike, rower or walk, then leg swings, hip circles, band pull-aparts and arm circles. Before the first exercise of the day, do 2-3 lighter ramp-up sets (about 50%, 70% and 85% of your working weight) before your working sets.', '{"1": "Upper", "2": "Lower", "3": "Pu